Subject: Quote native bootstrap runfiles paths

Applies to: rules_python 2.4.5, python/private/stage1_bootstrap_template.sh.

Observed failure: a relocated runtime distribution under a path containing
spaces fails with "Python interpreter not found: debug". Unquoted arguments
split RUNFILES_DIR before find_python_interpreter receives it. Automatic
runfiles discovery and symlink traversal have the same argument-splitting issue.

Rationale and scope: quote these three paths in the non-zip bootstrap path.
Retain interpreter selection, runfiles lookup, environment and exec behavior.
No changes to zip extraction, runtime-created venvs or toolchain selection.

Verification: the regression suite in //third_party/rules_python:bootstrap_test
exercises relocated execution with explicit/automatic runfiles and a symlinked
launcher; all three subcases pass with --config=runtime --config=no-agnocast.
The test packages the actual native bootstrap/interpreter and runs it from a
different working directory. It does not exercise zip or runtime-created venvs.

Upstream: the same unquoted calls remain in the main-branch template inspected
2026-11-23; no matching fix association is recorded.
https://github.com/bazel-contrib/rules_python/blob/main/python/private/stage1_bootstrap_template.sh

--- a/python/private/stage1_bootstrap_template.sh
+++ b/python/private/stage1_bootstrap_template.sh
@@ -124 +124 @@
-      stub_filename=$(readlink $stub_filename)
+      stub_filename=$(readlink "$stub_filename")
@@ -129 +129 @@
-  RUNFILES_DIR=$(find_runfiles_root $0)
+  RUNFILES_DIR=$(find_runfiles_root "$0")
@@ -151 +151 @@
